IX. BACKUP AND SUPPLEMENTAL ASSIGNMENTS
A. Circuit judges are authorized to supplement and aid the county court in the county to which 
the circuit judge is assigned.  Circuit judges are also authorized to supplement and aid any 
other circuit or county judge in the circuit when they are unavailable, requests assistance, 
or assigned by the Chief Judge.
B. County judges are temporarily assigned to supplement circuit court.  County judges shall 
not be assigned to handle contested family law cases or child support cases except in an 
emergency.
C. County judges in each of the counties may handle uncontested family matters and 
simplified dissolution of marriage cases in consultation with the assigned circuit judge.
D. When necessary for the orderly administration of the Second Judicial Circuit, and for the 
prompt dispatch of the business of the court, the Chief Judge may assign senior judges to 
temporary service in any court of the Second Judicial Circuit, with the authority to hear, 
conduct, try, determine, and dispose of the cases and matters presented to him or her.
E. Jury Qualification.
1. Circuit judges assigned to Franklin, Gadsden, Jefferson, Liberty, and Wakulla 
Counties shall be responsible for qualifying the jury venire during their trial weeks.
2. County judges in Franklin, Gadsden, Jefferson, Liberty, and Wakulla Counties shall 
qualify jurors during their trial weeks.
3. Leon County judges shall qualify Leon County jurors on a rotating basis as determined 
by the Leon County Administrative Judge.
F. Children Services Council of Leon County.  Circuit Judge Barbara K. Hobbs is appointed 
to the Children’s Services Council of Leon County, pursuant to section 125.901(1)(a), 
Florida Statutes.
X. MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS
A. Courtrooms and hearing rooms shall be assigned by the Office of Court Administration, 
in consultation with the Chief Judge.
B. All judges assigned to new divisions shall assume the caseload, opened or reopened, 
previously assigned to the preceding judge, including all pending and scheduled hearings, 
proceedings, trial dates, and associated scheduling matters, unless otherwise directed by 
the Chief Judge.
C. Judges may agree among themselves to exchange duty weeks or otherwise arrange 
coverage with other judges in the Second Circuit.
D. Effective Date: This Second Amendment shall be effective immediately and shall 
supersede Administrative Order 2026-02, First Amendment.
DONE AND ORDERED in chambers in Tallahassee, Leon County, Florida, this 21st day of August 
